      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::central-data-lake/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::central-data-lake"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/TenantId": "${aws:userid}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of private AWS data access patterns, policy composition, and practical testing. 

## Key Concepts
- S3 public access blocking and bucket policy conditions
- VPC Endpoints and endpoint policies
- aws:SourceVpce condition and VPCE validation
- IAM roles for data producers

## Code Example
```
# Bucket policy (allow via VPCE)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceVpce": "vpce-abc123"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```
# VPCE policy (minimal, allows basic access to bucket)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*"]
    }
  ]
}
```
```
# IAM role for producer (trusts producer principal)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {"Effect": "Allow","Action": ["s3:PutObject"],"Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*"}
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to multiple VPCEs per environment?
- How would you monitor and audit VPCE access over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design data residency controls, cross-region analytics, and automated tenant lifecycle in a scalable, secure way. Requires reasoning about IAM boundaries, per-tenant data segregation, and disaster recovery trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency and tenant isolation
- Region-bound storage and access controls
- Serverless analytics stack (Lambda, Glue, Athena/Redshift)
- Automated onboarding/offboarding (CDK/Terraform)
- Cross-region dashboards and DR strategy (RTO/RPO)

## Code Example

```javascript
// CDK sketch (simplified)
const bucket = new s3.Bucket(this, 'TenantBucket', {
  encryption: s3.BucketEncryption.S3_MANAGED,
  removalPolicy: RemovalPolicy.RETAIN
});
